GhostTab is fully built. Here's a summary of everything created:

---

**Application** (`dist/`)

- `core.mjs` — pure business logic: URL validation, parsing, deduplication, queue management, progress, export, localStorage serialisation with full shape validation. Zero DOM dependencies.
- `style.css` — haunted library theme: near-black plum `#1a1020`, ivory type, lavender accents, CSS ghost silhouette drawn with `clip-path` polygon + radial gradient on `body::before`, floating animation paused under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- `app.js` — DOM controller: all events, keyboard shortcuts (O/R/S), localStorage persist/restore, `textContent`-only mutations, `noopener,noreferrer` tab opening, clipboard export with textarea fallback.
- `index.html` — buildless single page: semantic `<section>` panels, `aria-live` regions, `role="progressbar"`, no external CDN, `<script type="module">`.

**Tests**

```
node --test tests/core.test.mjs
ℹ tests 48  ·  ℹ pass 48  ·  ℹ fail 0
```

**Documentation**

- `.kiro/specs/ghosttab/` — requirements, design (architecture, security, decisions log), tasks
- `.kiro/steering/product.md` — product purpose and principles
- `LICENSE` (MIT, 2026 Matias Luparia), `README.md`
- `submission/description.md` and `submission/demo-script.md` — both clearly marked **DRAFT — not submitted**; no video claimed
